  "crlf_lf_relationship": "Git stores text files with LF. When Python on Windows writes text files via the default 'open' mode (newline=None), it uses the platform-native CRLF. The execution-time SHA-256 (CRLF) is what the runner saw; the repository-byte SHA-256 (LF) is what Git stores. The two hashes differ when the file contains any newline character; the relationship is: sha256_crlf = sha256(content with CRLF), sha256_lf = sha256(content with LF)."
